+
+# Plan: precise, framework-aware default knowledge
+
+Status: working plan, measured on `engine/package-scoped-facts` at `b23076c`
+(`0.8.0-beta`) against `0.7.0`. Written so a contributor or agent can pick up one
+work item at a time.
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+The engine should report only what it can stand behind, and say so when it
+cannot know. Default knowledge lives in `frensense-lang` and `frensense-packgen`
+so that major bugs are caught without a corpus; corpora and `.frc` bundles add
+detections on top. Concretely:
+
+- A name alone never makes something a sink. A sink fires when the receiver's
+  origin (package, type) is resolved, or when the entry is explicitly marked as
+  safe to match by name (for example global `eval`).
+- Framework awareness changes which sources, sinks and sanitizers apply. It does
+  not mute dangerous built-ins: `eval(tainted)` must fire in Next.js and Nuxt too.
+- Unknown is reported as unknown (coverage output), not as clean.
+
+## 2. How to classify a problem
+
+Ask in this order and stop at the first yes. Every work item below carries one
+primary layer.
+
+| Layer | Owns | Typical fix | Files |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **LANG** | Syntax or structure the engine cannot currently see: decorators and parameter annotations, typed extractors in Rust parameter patterns, route attributes, declared types of receivers, import forms and aliases, `::` call paths, tagged templates | Extend `LanguageSpec` and the provider so the IR carries the fact | `frensense-lang/src/spec.rs`, `frensense-lang/src/providers/*` |
+| **KNOWLEDGE** | Names and shapes the engine already understands: sources, sinks, sanitizers, propagators, per-slot signatures, package-scoped entries, validator names, misuse-rule data | Add or fix a table entry; could a corpus fact fix it? then it is knowledge | `frensense-packgen/src/vocab/**`, `frensense-packgen/src/data.rs`, then regenerate the default pack |
+| **ENGINE** | Analysis semantics: receiver origin, flow joins, guards, sink gating, confidence, checks without data flow, explain output | Change analysis code. It must stay free of library and framework names (purity ratchet) | `frensense-engine/src/analysis/**`, `ir/lowering/**`, `checks/**` |
+
+Tie-breakers:
+
+1. If the information is not in the IR (a decorator, a type annotation, a path
+   prefix), the first fix is **LANG**, even if a table entry follows.
+2. If a table entry exists but the engine cannot consume its shape (for example a
+   propagator rule that matches only the last name segment), the first fix is
+   **ENGINE**.
+3. A misuse check with no source-to-sink flow (weak PRNG, cookie flags, XXE
+   parser settings) is **ENGINE** (`checks/`) plus **KNOWLEDGE** (rule data).
+4. A policy question (should an argv element be reported as command injection?)
+   is a **DECISION** for the maintainers, not a code task.
+
+How to prove a label before starting (do this, do not guess):
+
+1. Minimise the case to one file.
+2. Search the vocab tables for the name. Present in the table and still failing?
+   Then it is not a plain knowledge gap.
+3. Vary one thing: rename the receiver variable, call the function bare vs
+   path-qualified, swap the source for a known one, move the code out of the
+   handler. The thing that flips the result names the layer.
+4. Compare with `0.7.0`. A case that passed there and fails now is a regression
+   and goes first.
+
+## 3. Current measurements
+
+| Check | `0.7.0` | branch |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `scripts/framework_matrix.py` (148 cases) | n/a | 98 pass; open: 29 knowledge, 17 lang, 4 engine as labelled |
+| `tests/framework_matrix_extra` (98 cases) | 60 of 96 | 64 of 98; open: 11 knowledge, 12 lang, 8 engine, 3 decision |
+| OWASP BenchmarkPython, conservative, bare | TPR 25.7%, FPR 1.5% (TP 116, FP 12) | TPR 27.7%, FPR 3.9% (TP 125, FP 30) |
+| Unit tests | | 561 passed, 0 failed (run was finishing) |
+
+What the branch fixed: Prisma `$queryRawUnsafe` with import origin; Drizzle
+`sql` tag false positive; the Python if/else-assign probe; `lxml` `.xpath()` sink; CWE tags
+for `eval`/`exec` and open redirects; unrelated-receiver `execute` in Python.
+
+What it regressed or exposed (all verified):
+
+- **Receiver origin depends on variable names.** `x = sqlite3.connect(...);
+  x.execute(...)` is silent on the branch for any name outside the allowlist
+  derived from the sink tables (`conn`, `cur`, `db`, `cursor`). Passes on `0.7.0`.
+  Same shape in JS (`const x = new Pool()`) is silent on both versions.
+- **New false positives**: 16 safe XPath cases (inline guard
+  `if "'" in bar: return`) and 2 `eval` cases now fire because their sinks are
+  newly recognised and the guards are not understood.
+- **`--explain` reports "0 silent sink arguments"** for the silent
+  `x.execute(...)` case, so the loud-failure output does not yet cover unresolved
+  receivers.
+
+## 4. Corrections to the matrix labels
+
+`scripts/framework_matrix.py` assigns layers from hints written into each case.
+These were checked against the tables and by experiment:
+
+| Case | Matrix label | Correct primary layer | Evidence |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `py-sqlite-concat` | KNOWLEDGE sink | ENGINE (receiver origin) | `execute` appears 19 times in the sink tables; `conn`/`cur`/`db` fire, `x`/`e`/`r`/`c` do not; passes on 0.7.0 |
+| `rs-fs-read`, `rs-redirect`, `rs-rusqlite-format` | KNOWLEDGE sink | LANG first (no Rust source is recognised), then ENGINE (`::` call paths) | `read_to_string` is in the table; bare `read_to_string(&p)` fires but `std::fs::read_to_string(&p)` does not |
+| `src-next-url-searchparams`, `src-next-nexturl`, `src-next-cookies`, `src-next-headers` | KNOWLEDGE | KNOWLEDGE, blocked on ENGINE | `PropagatorRule` matches only the last name segment, so `.get` cannot be scoped to `Request`/`URLSearchParams` without making every `Map.get` a propagator |
+| `go-unrelated-query` | ENGINE | LANG + ENGINE | the receiver's type comes from its declaration (`var db *sql.DB`), which the spec does not expose |
+| `py-django-filter` | KNOWLEDGE | KNOWLEDGE (confirmed) | `filter` is registered as a name-only SQL sink (`python.rs`); Django ORM `filter()` is parameterised |
+
+## 5. Work items
+
+Order matters: items marked **blocks** unblock others. Each item names its primary
+layer, the cases that must flip, and the constraints that must keep holding.
+
+### Phase 0: stop losing recall
+
+**WI-01 [ENGINE] Receiver origin from dataflow, not names. Blocks WI-02, WI-04, WI-10.**
+Resolve a receiver's origin by following assignments and calls: `x = pkg.factory(...)`,
+chained calls (`.cursor()`), `new Pkg()`, aliases (`y = x`), values stored in
+fields. Replace the `client_roots` name allowlist in `walk.rs` (receiver-root
+resolution around lines 415 to 520) and the verb gating in
+`facts/signatures.rs::is_sink_call_scoped`. Factory special cases (`create`,
+`extend`) become one rule: a call on an imported package yields a value with that
+package as origin.
+- Must flip: `py28_receiver_name_x`, `js36_receiver_name_x`, `py-sqlite-concat`, `rs-rusqlite-format`.
+- Must keep: `py08_unrelated_execute`, `js03_unrelated_unsafe_method`, `js06_unrelated_query`, `go14_unrelated_query` stay silent.
+- Test: a table-driven test that runs the same snippet with ten receiver names and asserts identical results.
+
+### Phase 1: knowledge (no engine change; regenerate the pack and run the drift check)
+
+**WI-02 [KNOWLEDGE] Package roots per language** for the clients the engine should treat as origins: `sqlite3`, `psycopg2`, `pymysql`, `sqlalchemy`, `requests`, `httpx`, `database/sql`, `gorm.io/gorm`, `sqlx`, `rusqlite`, `diesel`, `pg`, `mysql2`, `knex`, `typeorm`, `sequelize`, `@prisma/client`, `drizzle-orm`. Depends on WI-01.
+
+**WI-03 [KNOWLEDGE, blocked on WI-18] JS request sources.** `new URL(req.url).searchParams.get`, `req.nextUrl.searchParams.get`, `req.cookies.get`, `req.headers.get` for Next; the h3/Nuxt equivalents already work for `getQuery`. Cases: `src-next-*`, `js10_next_searchparams_prisma`, `js16_next_nexturl_prisma`.
+
+**WI-04 [KNOWLEDGE] JS sinks, package-scoped.** `sql.raw` (drizzle-orm), `knex().raw`, TypeORM `DataSource.query`/`EntityManager.query`, Mongoose `$where`, DOM `innerHTML` with `location.hash` as a source. Each as an entry with a package (the `JS_PACKAGE_SCOPED_SINKS` shape), and the safe pair left silent (`sql` tag, `raw(sql, bindings)`, `textContent`). Cases: `js05`, `js18`, `js32`, `js-typeorm-query-concat`, `js-mongoose-where`.
+
+**WI-05 [KNOWLEDGE] Python.** Remove or scope `filter` (Django ORM); add `requests`/`httpx` `get|post|request` as SSRF sinks; add `secure_filename` and `os.path.basename` as path sanitizers; add `request.get_json` and FastAPI `request.query_params`/`headers` as sources. Cases: `py06`, `py20`, `py22`, `py-requests-ssrf`, `py-secure-filename`, `py-basename`, `src-flask-json`, `src-fastapi-request`.
+
+**WI-06 [KNOWLEDGE] Go.** gorm `Raw`/`Exec`/`Where` scoped to `gorm.io/gorm`; `filepath.Base` as a path sanitizer; `r.Cookie`, chi `URLParam`, mux `Vars` as sources; `Fprintf(w, ...)` and `w.Write` as XSS sinks (needs WI-15 first to avoid JSON-API false positives). Cases: `go04`, `go09`, `go11`, `go-gorm-*`, `go-filepath-base`, `src-nethttp-cookie`, `src-chi-urlparam`, `src-mux-vars`.
+
+**WI-07 [KNOWLEDGE, blocked on WI-09, WI-11] Rust.** `sqlx::query*`, `diesel::sql_query`, `rusqlite` execute and query, `Redirect::to`, `Html(...)` as sinks; integer `parse` as a sanitizer. Cases: `rs01`, `rs08`, `rs11`, `rs13`, `rs-parse-cast`, `rs-sqlx-format`, `rs-diesel-sql-query`.
+
+### Phase 2: language packs
+
+**WI-08 [LANG] Decorator and annotation aware parameter taint.** Pass decorators and parameter annotations to `classify_param_taint` (today it receives name and type only): Nest `@Query()`, `@Body()`, `@Param()`, `@Headers()`; FastAPI typed route parameters, `Query()`, `Header()`, `Cookie()`, pydantic body models; Flask `<converter:name>` route parameters. Gate on the route decorator, not on the parameter name. Cases: `js15_nest_decorator_direct`, `py07_fastapi_param_sqlite`, `src-nest-*`, `src-fastapi-*`, `src-flask-route-param`.
+
+**WI-09 [LANG] Rust typed extractors.** Treat `Query(p): Query<T>`, `web::Query<T>`, `Path`, `Json`, `Form`, `HeaderMap`, and Rocket route attributes as request input in `classify_param_taint`. Cases: `rs01` through `rs14`, `src-axum-*`, `src-actix-*`, `src-rocket-param`. Add a recognised baseline source to each Rust frame in `framework_matrix.py` so sink cases stop falling back.
+
+**WI-10 [LANG, then ENGINE] Declared types as origin.** Expose a receiver's declared type: Go `var db *sql.DB`, TS constructor parameters (`private readonly prisma: PrismaService`) with `class PrismaService extends PrismaClient` resolved across files, Python annotations, Rust `State<PgPool>`. The engine feeds it into WI-01's origin value. Cases: `js14_nest_di_prisma`, `nest-prisma-injected`, `go14_unrelated_query`.
+
+**WI-11 [LANG or ENGINE; investigate first] Rust `::` call paths.** Make `std::fs::read_to_string(..)` and `fs::read_to_string(..)` match the entry that matches bare `read_to_string(..)`. Normalise through `use` imports in the spec, or match on the last `::` segment in the engine; pick whichever keeps the engine free of Rust-specific names. Cases: `rs05_fs_read`, `rs-fs-read`.
+
+### Phase 3: engine precision
+
+**WI-12 [ENGINE + KNOWLEDGE] Global vs method calls.** Let a table entry say "global only" so `eval(x)` fires and `engine.eval(x)` does not, unless the receiver origin is known. Case: `js-unrelated-eval-method`.
+
+**WI-13 [ENGINE + KNOWLEDGE] Guard predicates.** A guard that dominates the sink and constrains the value should clear taint: allowlist `.includes()`, `str.isdigit()`/`isalnum()`, `in` containment with a constant, full-match regex, and the apostrophe check behind the 16 new XPath false positives. Add a packgen table of validator names (extend `BOOTSTRAP_CONTAINMENT_CALLEES`) and have the engine use it. Cases: `py27`, `py-guard-isalnum`, `js-guard-includes`, and the 16 CWE-643 benchmark cases.
+
+**WI-14 [ENGINE] Joins.** Taint through if/else assignment joins in Python (`py24`) and Go (`go17`); the JS case (`js35`) passes. The branch's merge fix (`d441bad`) closed the simpler probe shape only. Then `match`/`switch`. Cases: `py24_join_if_else`, `go17_if_else_join`, `join: match assign` probe.
+
+**WI-15 [ENGINE] Content-type aware XSS.** A write to a response is an XSS sink only when the content type is HTML or unset. Required for WI-06's Go entries and for Express `res.send` vs `res.json` (already correct).
+
+### Phase 4: checks without data flow
+
+**WI-17 [ENGINE `checks/` + KNOWLEDGE rule data]** Weak PRNG used for tokens (CWE-330/338), cookie `secure`/`httponly` flags (CWE-614/1004), permissive XML parser settings (CWE-611). Rule data in `frensense-packgen/src/data.rs`; check code in `frensense-engine/src/checks/`. Cases: `py25`, `py26`, `go18`.
+
+### Cross-cutting
+
+**WI-18 [ENGINE] Receiver-qualified propagators.** Let a propagator rule name a receiver type or origin so `.get` propagates only on `Request`, `URLSearchParams`, `Headers`. Unblocks WI-03.
+
+**WI-19 [ENGINE] Loud failure.** `--explain` and the MCP result list sink-like calls whose receiver origin was not resolved, files or frameworks with no pack, and sources not recognised. A clean result carries a coverage summary.
+
+**WI-20 [ENGINE + KNOWLEDGE] Confidence tiers.** Name-only evidence (parameter named `req`, `c`, `e`, `r`) gets a lower confidence value than type- or decorator-backed evidence. Keep the existing `confidence` field and `min_confidence` argument; do not delete name-based sources.
+
+**WI-21 [KNOWLEDGE] CWE tags on every sink.** The new XPath sink has no CWE, so scoring and reports cannot attribute it. Add a tag test that fails when a sink label has no CWE mapping.
+
+**DECISIONS needed (WI-16).** Report an argv element in `subprocess.run([...])`, `exec.Command(...)` or `execFile(...)` as command injection (CWE-78), as argument injection (CWE-88) at lower severity, or not at all? Cases: `py09`, `go07`, `js23` expect silence today; change the expectation if the answer changes.
+
+## 6. Rules for whoever picks this up
+
+1. One work item per PR. Do not bundle release, version or docs-site changes with engine work.
+2. Every new scoped fact needs three tests, run through the CLI (the unit harness treated `bad(email: string)` as a source where the CLI does not): fires with the right origin, silent on an unrelated receiver, silent on a wrong-package look-alike.
+3. Before opening the PR run: `scripts/local-ci.sh`; `python3 scripts/framework_matrix.py --bin <new> --compare-bin <0.7.0 binary>`; `python3 tests/framework_matrix_extra/run.py --bin <new> --compare-bin <0.7.0 binary>`; the OWASP scorer with `--baseline --fail-on-regression`; `triage_misses.py --probes-only`.
+4. The matrix lists may only shrink: when a case starts passing, remove it from the xfail or `known_gaps.json` list in the same PR. A newly failing case that is not listed is a regression and blocks the PR.
+5. Do not tune entries against OWASP BenchmarkPython. Add a minimal real-world fixture for each change instead.
+6. Keep library and framework names out of `frensense-engine`; the purity ratchet enforces it. Names belong in packgen or a bundle.
+7. If a new sink makes a safe case fire, fix the cause (guard, sanitizer, origin) or leave the entry out. Do not suppress the case.
+
+## 7. Where the cases live
+
+- `scripts/framework_matrix.py`: frame/source/sink matrix with automatic source, sink and flow decomposition. Its layer labels come from case hints; see section 4 for corrections.
+- `tests/framework_matrix_extra/`: 98 fixtures covering joins, guards, misuse checks, DOM sinks, argv handling and receiver-name independence. `known_gaps.json` records the layer, work item and evidence level (`verified` = confirmed by experiment or table inspection, `inferred` = from code reading; confirm before starting).
